<div class="sc-hero-band" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:#fff;position:relative;z-index:1;overflow:hidden;"><div class="cap-section cap-section--band cap-section--hero" style="padding-bottom:0;"><div style="margin-bottom:64px;">
    <div style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--hana-blue);margin-bottom:14px;">OSAT · QFN, DFN &amp; LGA</div>
    <h1 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:46px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-0.03em;margin:0 0 18px;max-width:740px;text-wrap:balance;">QFN, DFN &amp; LGA</h1>
    <p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:18px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 32px;text-wrap:pretty;">Through consistent investment in manufacturing technologies and package design, Hana has developed market leading capabilities in QFN, DFN and LGA packages across a broad range of body sizes, thicknesses and lead configurations. Wettable-flank processing, thin-body molding and multi-die integration are available for more demanding designs.</p>
    <div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface);width:100%;height:407px;"><img src="~/images/qfn-hero.jpg" alt="QFN, DFN and LGA leadless packages" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center;"></div>
    <div class="hana-spec-block" style="margin-top:18px;"><div class="hana-spec-item"><div class="hana-spec-label" style="display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">Wettable flank solutions</div><div class="hana-spec-value" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:17px;">2 types</div></div><div class="hana-spec-item"><div class="hana-spec-label" style="display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">In-house chemical de-burr</div><div class="hana-spec-value" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:17px;">50 µm</div></div><div class="hana-spec-item"><div class="hana-spec-label" style="display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">Film-assist mold thickness</div><div class="hana-spec-value" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:17px;">0.9 mm</div></div><div class="hana-spec-item"><div class="hana-spec-label" style="display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">Multi-die QFN, zero delamination</div><div class="hana-spec-value" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:17px;">MSL1</div></div></div>
  </div></div></div>
<div class="sc-pillars-band" data-hana-bg="wafer" data-variant="light" data-accent="" data-fade="none" style="background:linear-gradient(120deg,#f5f7fa 35%,#d8e6f3 100%);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="cap-section cap-section--band"><div style="margin-bottom:64px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Capability overview</h2><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:15.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:640px;margin:10px 0 0;">Our leadless packaging capability covers wettable-flank finishing, thin-body molding, and multi-die integration.</p></div><div class="cap-grid-3"><div class="sc-pillar" style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;"><div style="padding:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1;"><div style="width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--hana-blue);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:14px;"><i data-lucide="scan-line" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin-bottom:10px;">Automotive finish</div><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 16px;">Wettable-flank finishes for automated optical inspection.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 16px;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Step-cut wettable flank for full-lead QFN</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Single-cut wettable flank for dimple-on-lead QFN</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Chemical de-burr capability to 50 µm</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Both wettable-flank methods in production</span></li></ul></div></div><div class="sc-pillar" style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;"><div style="padding:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1;"><div style="width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--hana-blue);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:14px;"><i data-lucide="layers" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin-bottom:10px;">Mold &amp; build</div><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 16px;">Thin-body construction with controlled planarity.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 16px;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Film-assist molding at 0.9 mm body thickness</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Copper-clip QFN and DFN assembly</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Flip-chip QFN and DFN assembly</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Solder screen printing with SAC305 and PdSnAg</span></li></ul></div></div><div class="sc-pillar" style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;"><div style="padding:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1;"><div style="width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--hana-blue);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:14px;"><i data-lucide="square-stack" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin-bottom:10px;">Multi-die</div><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 16px;">Heterogeneous multi-die integration in a single leadless body.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 16px;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Two FETs and one IC integrated side by side</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Zero top-side delamination on CSAM</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Vacuum reflow with controlled voiding</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Support for heterogeneous device combinations</span></li></ul></div></div></div></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:32px;"><div style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--hana-blue);margin-bottom:12px;">Also on this line</div><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 12px;text-wrap:balance;">Unit-level traceability</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:15px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:600px;margin:0 0 18px;">Each unit is traceable through assembly and test, so a leadless package can be tied back to its lot, line and process record.</p><a href="/capabilities/automation/mes-traceability" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hana-blue);text-decoration:none;" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MES and traceability <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></div></div>
<div style="background:var(--surface);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="cap-section"><div style="display:grid;gap:44px;"><div style="border-top:2px solid var(--hana-blue);padding-top:14px;"><div style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--hana-blue);margin-bottom:10px;">Method</div><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:21px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 10px;text-wrap:balance;">Two wettable flank methods</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:14.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 22px;max-width:680px;">A step cut for full-lead QFN and a single cut for dimple-on-lead, both in production and both giving automated optical inspection a visible fillet for automotive joint-inspection requirements.</p><div class="why-media" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;"><div style="overflow:hidden;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:#0a1f3a;aspect-ratio:1448/1086;"><img src="~/images/qfn-step-cut.jpg" alt="Step cut wettable flank on a full-lead QFN" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain;"></div><div style="overflow:hidden;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:#0a1f3a;aspect-ratio:1448/1086;"><img src="~/images/qfn-dimple.jpg" alt="Dimple-on-lead wettable flank" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain;"></div></div></div><div style="border-top:2px solid var(--hana-blue);padding-top:14px;"><div style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--hana-blue);margin-bottom:10px;">Chemistry</div><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:21px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 10px;text-wrap:balance;">In-house de-burr chemistry</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:14.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 22px;max-width:680px;">The de-burr chemistry is developed and controlled by us, so lead finishing stays inside the same production operation as the flank cut.</p><div style="overflow:hidden;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:#0a1f3a;aspect-ratio:1672/941;"><img src="~/images/qfn-chemical-deburr.jpg" alt="Copper burrs before and after chemical de-burr" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain;"></div></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Where we run it</h2><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:15.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:640px;margin:10px 0 0;">Leadless assembly is available across our OSAT network; production mix varies by site.</p></div><div class="cap-grid-4"><a href="/locations/ayutthaya" style="text-decoration:none;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);padding:22px;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;"><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;margin-bottom:7px;"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:14px;height:14px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--hana-blue);">Thailand</span></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Ayutthaya</div></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hana-blue);">Explore Ayutthaya <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a><a href="/locations/jiaxing" style="text-decoration:none;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);padding:22px;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;"><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;margin-bottom:7px;"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:14px;height:14px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--hana-blue);">China</span></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Jiaxing</div></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hana-blue);">Explore Jiaxing <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;"><details class="sc-faq" open><summary>Do you offer wettable flanks?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Yes, in two forms — a step cut for full-lead QFN and a single cut for dimple-on-lead QFN. Both run in production, with chemical de-burr to 50 µm.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>What sizes and lead counts do you run?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">DFN from 0.6 × 1.0 mm, QFN to 12 × 12 mm, and LGA from 1.0 × 1.5 × 0.5 mm — the full standard range is searchable in the package reference on this page.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>Can you put more than one die in a leadless package?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Yes — two FETs and an IC side by side in a single body, passing MSL1 with zero top delamination on CSAM.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>What is the difference between the two wettable flank cuts?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">The step cut suits a full-lead QFN, where material is removed to form a step that supports solder wetting along the lead edge. The single cut suits a dimple-on-lead design and uses de-burr chemistry to leave the lead clean.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>Does a thinner body change what you can put inside it?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">It changes the die thickness and the loop clearance, not the package family. The thickness ladder runs from 0.37 mm to 0.90 mm as standard, with film-assist molding used to control planarity and warpage in thin package bodies.</div></details></div></div></div></div>
